# Rules authoring

The oh-my-cursor plugin has two rule scopes and they are intentionally
distinct.

## Scopes

| Scope | Path | Ships with `install-local-plugin.ts`? | When to use |
|-------|------|----------------------------------------|-------------|
| Plugin-shipped | `rules/*.mdc` | YES — copied into `~/.cursor/plugins/local/oh-my-cursor/rules/` | Rules that should apply in every consumer workspace that installs this plugin |
| Workspace dev-only | `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` | NO — explicitly excluded by `--exclude='/.cursor/rules/'` in `install-local-plugin.ts` | Rules that govern editing this repo (docs claims, commit discipline, error handling, memory templates) |

The exclude in the install script is deliberate. Workspace dev rules tell
the *maintainer* what to do when editing this repository; they would be
noise in consumer workspaces that install this plugin.

## Frontmatter shape

Every `.mdc` rule starts with a YAML frontmatter block:

```mdc
---
description: "[OMCS] <one-sentence purpose, present tense, ASCII only>"
globs:
	- <path glob 1>
	- <path glob 2>
alwaysApply: <true|false>
---
```

- `description` starts with `[OMCS] ` for plugin-shipped rules. Workspace
  dev rules omit the bracket prefix and use a short title (see
  `.cursor/rules/00-repo-scope.mdc`).
- `globs` use forward slashes, may contain `**`, and are tab-indented.
- `alwaysApply: true` only for repo-wide invariants. Default to `false`
  with explicit globs.

## Validators that gate a new rule

Run every time a rule is added or edited:

| Validator | What it checks |
|-----------|-----------------|
| `scripts/validate-plugin-structure.sh` | New plugin-shipped rule must be listed in the `required` array if it is part of the contract |
| `scripts/validate-rules-install-parity.sh` | Every `rules/*.mdc` shipped in the repo is also present in the install payload (when `install-local-plugin.ts` is run) |
| `scripts/validate-agent-bridge-contract.ts` | Rules must not invoke the workflow-state writer CLI or reference archived doc paths |
| `scripts/validate-public-language.ts` | Rules must not contain validator-forbidden legacy package names |

## Anti-patterns

- Adding `alwaysApply: true` to a narrowly-scoped rule. Use globs.
- Editing `rules/*.mdc` to embed plugin behavior that should live in a
  `skills/<name>/SKILL.md` instead. Rules are short guidance; skills are
  invocable workflows.
- Documenting capabilities the plugin does not yet ship. Rules are
  evidence-backed (see `.cursor/rules/00-repo-scope.mdc`).
- Creating a workspace dev rule that consumers also need. Move it to
  `rules/` instead.
- Reformatting frontmatter with spaces instead of tabs. The existing rules
  use tab indentation; keep it consistent so downstream tooling matches.

